        <language>en</language>
        <item>
            <title>2.3</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 19:29:24 +1000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>10</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[
<ul>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">More reliable YouTube downloads. Apple Music links now work reliably</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">Optional "use one format for every service" setting: pick Audio or Video and a format once and it applies to every tab (off by default; each mode keeps its own setting otherwise)</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">Search results you have previewed stay highlighted, with the most recent one marked, so you can find your way back</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">The preview window Download button now shows the format you will get (MP3, MP4 and so on)</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">On the Search tab, right-click a Download button (in the list or the preview) to grab that result in a one-off format without changing your saved choice</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">On the Search tab, downloading a result keeps you on Search and marks it Added, so you can line up several without leaving the page</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">Queued playlists get ready in the background while they wait, so they start the moment their turn comes</li>
</ul>
            ]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/BSKapps/fetchpuppy-updates/releases/download/v2.3/Fetch.Puppy.2.3.zip" length="80908103" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="j/iooMFGKJIKaauuTkPmyGewXuc4KwXbqDEW44mlCanC0dGFyIh6dvAIVcI3hD/ZNf/aqjHTY6XqHFI7cGOlAw=="/>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title>2.2</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 22 Jun 2026 00:18:50 +1000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>9</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[
<ul>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">Rebuilt search preview/Added download button: streams load in the background as results appear, open faster, and play reliably</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">Now works on Intel Macs as well as Apple Silico</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">Each download row shows its actual format (MP3, AAC, MP4 and so on)</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">Drag several links at once to download them together, with faster track matching for Spotify, Apple Music and CSV</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">YouTube playlists now list every track, filling in as they load</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">Reddit and other social links that need browser cookies now download</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">Elapsed timer stops when a download finishes</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">MP3 downloads are now true 320 kbps CBR (were variable bitrate)</li>
<li style="margin-bottom:6px">YouTube playlists can be cancelled mid-download, and a failed playlist can be retried</li>
</ul>
            ]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/BSKapps/fetchpuppy-updates/releases/download/v2.2/Fetch.Puppy.2.2.zip" length="79668552" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="XWcTb+/K3gkKFb5n16dmX83LaOA1TeA1+xuFNMXgtLeJnjPSw8CpBJ4jyX3k+gxkWDbUUHLwdVUWrNoEm3d6AQ=="/>
        </item>
